    "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nPR 9 of #49569, the last step. It cleans up the leftover mypy errors in the parent test directories, then removes `\"tests\"` from `SEPARATE_GROUPS` so all of `tests/` is checked with `follow_imports=silent`.\r\n\r\nOpening as a draft while the work is in progress. **Do NOT merge until all PRs done in #49569.**\r\n\r\nCloses #49569\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\nProgress (counts from mypy 1.20.2, `--follow-imports silent`, on main as of 2026-10-21):\r\n\r\n- [x] `tests/compile`: 3 errors fixed, now enforced\r\n- [x] `tests/v1` loose files: 1 error fixed (enforced once `v1/core`, `v1/engine` and `v1/kv_connector` are done)\r\n- [ ] `tests/distributed`: 108 errors, mostly `DeviceCommunicatorBase | None`\r\n- [ ] `tests/models` loose files: 39 errors\r\n- [ ] `tests` root loose files: 41 errors, about half in `test_config.py`\r\n- [ ] Remove `tests`, `tests/models` and `tests/v1` from `SEPARATE_GROUPS`, and drop the `tests/**` entries from `SILENT_GROUPS`\r\n\r\nNo test behaviour changes. These are type fixes only.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nFor each directory, following the pattern in #49569:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nmypy --python-version 3.11 --follow-imports silent --warn-unused-ignores <dirs>\r\npre-commit run -a mypy\r\n```\r\n\r\nPlus a `group_files()` check that each moved directory routes to the `''` group.\r\n\r\nSo far: `tests/compile` and `tests/v1/test_serial_utils.py` are clean (64 files, no issues), and `ruff check` / `ruff format` pass. I didn't run the touched tests locally (no CUDA box), so CI is the check there.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n- `tests/compile` goes into `SILENT_GROUPS` as one entry and replaces its four sub-directory entries. Just deleting it from `SEPARATE_GROUPS` wouldn't do anything because the `tests` root group would still claim its files.\r\n- `tests/v1` can't go in `SILENT_GROUPS` yet. It's matched first, so it would enforce the unfinished sub-directories early.\r\n- One side effect: new test files added under an enforced directory get type-checked, so open PRs adding tests there may hit mypy errors on rebase.\r\n\r\nNot a duplicate. PR 9 is claimed in #49569, and no other open PR touches these directories or the\r\nmypy grouping.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\r\n",
